   "text": "This SMILES was read region by region from the drawing. The absolute configurations at the cyclohexane carbons were not checked against the wedges and are my assumption, so those two centres are the least certain part.\n\n- **Left pyridine:** a pyridine with the 2-carboxamide, a 4-vinyl group and a 5-OMe. The vinyl is drawn trans (E) and links to a cyclohexane.\n- **Cyclohexane:** a 1,4-disubstituted ring with the vinyl group on one carbon (hashed) and CF3 on the other (wedged). I took this as trans-1,4.\n- **Linker to the central aryl ring:** the amide N\u2013CH2 attaches to a meta-substituted benzene, which carries CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH.\n- **Alkyl chain:** NH\u2013(CH2)8\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH, counted as eight CH2 groups plus the carbonyl.\n- **Right-hand VHL ligand:** a tert-leucine unit, then a 4-hydroxyproline, then an amide to a benzyl group bearing a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl. I used the standard (2S,4R) VH032 stereo pattern for the proline and tert-leucine centres.\n\nSMILES: COc1cnc(cc1/C=C/[C@H]2CC[C@H](CC2)C(F)(F)F)C(=O)NCc3cccc(c3)CC(=O)NCCCCCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N4C[C@H](O)C[C@H]4C(=O)NCc5ccc(cc5)-c6scnc6C"
